  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0135_76d3f3570d91.png\" style=\"width: 228px; height: 260px;\" /></p><p>Equation&nbsp;of line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>Any point on the line is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;lies on the plane, so</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>For Image <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Distance of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;from the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>42</mn><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p>"
